ation of hospitalization, life-threatening illness, permanent disability, congenital anomaly or birth defect, or death.\"}, {\"loc\": \"table 1\", \"q\": \"†† Not mutually exclusive.\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"analytic_depth\", \"outcome_types\"]}", "type": "text"}]}